THOUGHT: Let me check if there are any issues with the error handling in the completeTransaction method. Looking at the code, I notice that when a transaction fails, it stores the error reason. However, there might be an issue with how the error reason is constructed when the content length exceeds the max error reason size. Let me look at this part more closely.

Looking at lines around 470-480 in proxy.go:
```go
errReason := "unknown error reason"
if contentLength > rp.maxErrorReasonSize {
    log.Infof("%s: Error reason length (%d) is greater than max error reason size (%d)", s, contentLength, rp.maxErrorReasonSize)
} else {
    errString, err := toString(reader)
    if err != nil {
        log.Errorf("%s failed to get error reason: %s", s, err.Error())
    }

    errReason = fmt.Sprintf("%s %s", failedTransactionPrefix, errString)
}
```

There seems to be an issue here. When contentLength > rp.maxErrorReasonSize, we only log a message but don't set errReason to anything specific. Then we pass this generic "unknown error reason" to completeTransaction. This could be improved by providing a more descriptive error message in this case.

Let me check the default value of MaxErrorReasonSize in the config to understand the context better.

```bash
find . -name "*.go" -exec grep -l "MaxErrorReasonSize" {} \;
```

